  <static seed="1817" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicAlgebra/FractionArithmetic/MultiplyFractions10.pg">
    <statement><p>Multiply: <m>\displaystyle{ \frac{2}{7} \cdot \frac{5}{9} }</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="7" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>{\frac{10}{63}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>To multiply two fractions, simply multiply both numerators and both denominators. We have:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 
\begin{aligned}[t]
   \frac{2}{7} \cdot \frac{5}{9}
           \amp = \frac{2 \cdot 5}{7 \cdot 9} \\
           \amp = \frac{10}{63}
\end{aligned}
    }</m></p>
<p>The answer to this question is <m>\displaystyle{\frac{10}{63}}</m>.</p>
</solution>
